WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.460
How do you prove that

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.400
a language is not context-free?

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.600
The context-free pumping lemma repeats

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.060
two pieces of a word

5
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.780
together, reflecting a repeated variable

6
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.840
in a parse tree. We

7
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.960
will apply it to three

8
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.580
equal blocks and keep its

9
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.160
quantifiers separate from the regular-language

10
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:18.620
version.

11
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.100
For a context-free language, every

12
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.920
sufficiently long member has a

13
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.500
split u v x y

14
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.420
z. The pieces v and

15
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.540
y are pumped by the

16
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.460
same exponent, at least one

17
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.600
is nonempty, and the entire

18
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.380
middle window v x y

19
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.840
has length at most p.

20
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.080
That window is not required

21
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.160
to begin at the start

22
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:39.700
of the input.

23
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.840
The parse-tree intuition explains why

24
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.620
two pieces repeat. A sufficiently

25
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.960
tall derivation repeats a variable

26
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.320
on one root-to-leaf path, and

27
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.160
replacing the smaller repeated-variable subtree

28
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.400
by the larger one adds

29
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.900
material on both sides. Removing

30
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.120
that outer expansion corresponds to

31
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.480
exponent zero, while repeating it

32
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.540
corresponds to larger exponents.

33
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.540
The formal proof uses a

34
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.980
smallest parse tree for the

35
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.660
chosen word and a repeated

36
00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.140
variable near the bottom of

37
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.120
a longest path. A bounded

38
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.760
branching factor gives a finite

39
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.340
pumping length and bounds the

40
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.260
selected subtree’s yield. Minimality prevents

41
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.800
both flanking yields from being

42
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.760
empty, because otherwise the larger

43
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.280
subtree could be removed without

44
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.140
changing the word.

45
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.980
Assume the three-equal-block language is

46
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.220
context-free and choose a to

47
00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.620
the p, b to the

48
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.300
p, c to the p.

49
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.800
It belongs to the language

50
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:34.820
and is long enough for

51
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.600
the lemma. Now take an

52
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.720
arbitrary permitted five-piece decomposition rather

53
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.420
than choosing favourable v and

54
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.080
y yourself.

55
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.980
A window of length at

56
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.620
most p cannot touch all

57
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.460
three blocks. Reaching an a

58
00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.680
and a c would already

59
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.560
require crossing all p copies

60
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.600
of b plus at least

61
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.620
two other symbols. Thus v

62
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.240
and y together can change

63
00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.540
counts in at most two

64
00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.440
adjacent blocks, leaving at least

65
00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.860
one count unchanged.

66
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.820
Pump with exponent two. If

67
00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.660
each pumped piece contains only

68
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.500
one symbol type, at least

69
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.500
one count increases because their

70
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.260
total length is positive, while

71
00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.300
an untouched count remains p.

72
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.280
The result cannot have all

73
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.080
three counts equal, so it

74
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.280
is outside the language.

75
00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.780
If either pumped piece crosses

76
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.120
a block boundary, repeating it

77
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.960
also introduces an out-of-order alternation

78
00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.640
such as b followed by

79
00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.900
a. Then the result fails

80
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.600
the required a-star b-star c-star

81
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.680
shape even before comparing counts.

82
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.140
These cases cover every legal

83
00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.480
decomposition, including a split with

84
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.860
one pumped piece empty.

85
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.020
The contradiction disproves the existence

86
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.080
of a context-free grammar for

87
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.780
this language. It does not

88
00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.760
say that one particular attempted

89
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.360
grammar happened to fail. The

90
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.520
bounded window and synchronized exponent

91
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.200
are the structural facts making

92
00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.160
the impossibility argument work.

93
00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.720
Things to take note of.

94
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.580
State the five-piece lemma with

95
00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.120
a bounded middle window, pump

96
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.240
v and y by the

97
00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.240
same exponent, and allow either

98
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.280
one to be empty but

99
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.660
not both. Verify witness membership,

100
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.360
handle every window case, and

101
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.400
identify an explicit count or

102
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.160
order violation rather than saying

103
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.280
the pieces look different.
